{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.minpoly_one_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.minpoly_one_add","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.lean#L102-L106","doc":"The minimal polynomial of `1 + w` (namely `4cos²(π/7)`) is\n`v³ − 5v² + 6v − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.minpoly_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.minpoly_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.lean#L96-L100","doc":"The minimal polynomial of `1 − w` (namely `−2cos(2πk/7)`) is\n`u³ − u² − 2u + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.bloch_key","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.bloch_key","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.lean#L88-L94","doc":"At any root of `w³ − 2w² − w + 1` one has `(1 − w)²(1 + w) = w²`.\n\nThis is the identity behind `δ(2[w] + [−w]) = w ∧ w² = 0`, i.e. behind\n`2[w] + [−w]` lying in the Bloch group of `ℚ(ζ₇)⁺`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.bloch_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.bloch_poly","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The sharp form.** `(1 − w)²(1 + w) − w²` is *identically* the minimal\npolynomial `w³ − 2w² − w + 1` of `w = 1 + 2cos(2πk/7)`.\n\nSo the Bloch-group condition is not a consequence of the minimal polynomial —\nit is the same polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.prod_x_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.prod_x_sub","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.lean#L65-L75","doc":"`∏ⱼ (x − yⱼ) = x²` — the cleared form of `∏ⱼ (1 − yⱼ/x) = 1/x`.\n\nTogether with `prod_one_sub_x_mul` this gives\n`∏ⱼ [(1 − yⱼ/x)/(1 − x·yⱼ)] = 1/x²`, which is what turns the envelope\nderivative into `−2·log x / x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.prod_one_sub_x_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.prod_one_sub_x_mul","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCyclotomicBloch.lean#L54-L63","doc":"`∏ⱼ (1 − x·yⱼ) = x` for the roots of GGM's deformed 5₂ curve.\n\nHypotheses are Vieta for `x·y³ − (x²+1)·y² + (x²+x+1)·y − x = 0`, with the\ndenominators cleared so the statement lives over any `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}